<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">North Brabant</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">North Brabant is a province in the south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/s-hertogenbosch">'s-Hertogenbosch</a> as its capital and Eindhoven, Tilburg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breda">Breda</a> as its largest cities. It corresponds roughly to the northern part of the medieval Duchy of Brabant, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> conquered in the Eighty Years' War and ruled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/states-brabant">States Brabant</a>. It became a province after 1796 and is traditionally Catholic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-brabant.jpg" alt="North Brabant" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Noord-Brabant_in_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
